Patch 24: rank transform types with the cheap quantiser, not the trellis.

Standalone, against anchor 5d628d8 (current origin/av2-enc).

VERIFICATION STATUS, STATED UP FRONT: I could NOT make this fire on my test
clip. On 192x128, 2 frames, cpu-used=4 the output was bit-identical to baseline
(md5 c2a7fb30... both ways) and the runtime unchanged. That is the same
signature I have criticised in other patches, so treat the speedup claim below
as unverified.

The reason is likely scale rather than gating. The two call sites are reached
only when cpi->sf.tx_sf.tx_type_search.prune_tx_type_est_rd is set -- a speed-4
feature, so enabled in that run -- AND num_allowed > 2, i.e. more than two
transform types survive earlier pruning. On a 192x128 clip at qp=135 there are
few coefficients and few surviving types. On 4K CTC content num_allowed > 2
should be common. That is a hypothesis; the CTC run is what settles it, and if
the arm comes back bit-identical the patch is a no-op and should be dropped
rather than tuned.

THE FINDING BEHIND IT. A callgrind profile of the current encoder at cpu-used=4
puts trellis quantisation at about 47% of all instructions retired:

    av2_trellis_quant                     9.95%
    av2_decide_states_q1_avx2             7.47%
    av2_decide_states_avx2                5.86%
    av2_optimize_txb_new                  3.72%
    av2_get_rate_dist_def_luma_q1_avx2    3.31%
    av2_update_states_avx2                3.28%
    av2_get_rate_dist_def_luma_avx2       3.17%
    av2_find_best_path_avx2               2.89%
    av2_update_nbr_diagonal_avx2          2.86%
    av2_optimize_fsc_block                2.51%
                                         -------
                                         ~47%

For comparison, the forward transform is 6.2%, coefficient rate estimation
3.6%, and transform-type search 2.0%. Quantisation is larger than partition
search, mode search and the loop filters combined, and every patch produced on
this project so far has attacked something else.

av2_trellis_quant contains ZERO speed-feature references. It runs at full
strength at every preset and at every stage of the search, including inside
loops whose only purpose is to order candidates.

THE CHANGE. prune_txk_type and prune_txk_type_separ are transform-type RANKING
loops: they evaluate candidates only to order them into txk_map, after which
the survivors are re-evaluated properly. Both passed a literal 1 for
use_optimize_b, forcing the trellis on for every candidate, independently of the
skip_trellis decision that every other av2_setup_quant call site in the file
honours. This patch passes 0 instead, so ranking uses the cheap quantiser while
the real decision still uses the trellis.

The structural argument is the same one the two-pass partition search made for
shapes: rank cheaply, decide properly. Both paths return a rate and a distortion
for the same transform, so the ordering signal survives; what is skipped is the
state-space search that only matters once a type has been chosen.

-DAVM_TX_RANK_TRELLIS=1 restores the original behaviour exactly.

